{"name":"Breath of Spring","hex":"#e9e1a7","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"breath","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act or process of breathing.","A single act of breathing in or out; a breathing of air."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["voiceless, surd; contrasting with voice (breath sounds, voice sounds)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breath"},{"term":"spring","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move or burst forth.","To appear."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of springing: a leap, a jump.","The season of the year in temperate regions in which temperatures and daylight hours rise, and plants spring from the ground and into bloom and dormant animals spring to life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spring"}],"entries":[{"title":"Breath of Spring","blocks":[{"text":"Breath of Spring is a 1958 stage comedy written by Peter Coke. It depicts a group of hitherto highly respectable senior citizens who become embroiled in stealing valuable fur coats and using the proceeds for charity. The play opened in the West End of London and ran for 430 performances. It toured the British provinces and was produced in Australia and New Zealand. It was adapted for the cinema as Make Mine Mink and as a stage musical as 70, Girls, 70."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breath_of_Spring","wikidata":"Q139963173"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"breath":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9d/En-us-breath.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9d/En-us-breath.ogg/En-us-breath.ogg.mp3"}],"spring":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/14/En-uk-spring.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"http